EXTENSIONS

Extensions written against the documented extension API are your own work.
They are not derivative works of this software, and you may license and
distribute them on whatever terms you choose. The same holds for programs that
use this software only through its documented HTTP API, such as scripts,
automations and tools of your own.

The following extension materials are also licensed to you under the BSD
Zero Clause License (0BSD), whose text is at the end of this file:

  - the type definitions in docs/extensions.d.ts;
  - the code examples in the "Writing extensions" part of the user guide,
    docs/guide.html;
  - the extension test kit in tools/extension-kit/.

You may copy them into an extension and distribute them on any terms. The
restrictions above do not apply to them.

The extensions under extensions/bundled/, the sample extension in
extensions/bundled/hello-world/ among them, are licensed to you under the MIT
License, whose text is at the end of this file and in each extension's own
LICENSE file. You may copy, change and distribute them on its terms, which ask
that the copyright notice and the license text stay with every copy. The
restrictions above do not apply to them. A third-party component inside one of
them, such as the Marcellus font in extensions/bundled/theme-midnight/, keeps
its own license (see the NOTICE file).

